  "label": "User projected onto the man as the embodiment of 'America First' in elections",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual entity 'man' (Chris Christie) through the textual overlay 'america first!' and 'when it comes to elections'. The meme implies that the user (as a viewer or participant in the political discourse) is to identify with or see themselves as aligned with the man's representation of 'America First' ideology specifically within the context of elections. This projection is achieved through the analogical mapping where the man is personified as the exemplar of the slogan, inviting the user to project their own political stance or identification onto him.",
